('Git Version Control', 'Learn to use Git version control tools and team collaboration', 'This course systematically explains the usage of Git version control tools and team collaboration methods. From basic operations, branch management to conflict resolution, workflow practice, it comprehensively covers Git usage skills. Through multiple practice projects, it helps learners improve team collaboration efficiency.\n\nCourse Content:\n1. Git basic operations\n2. Branching and merging\n3. Remote repository management\n4. Conflict resolution\n5. Team collaboration workflows\n\nProject Practice:\n- Personal project version management\n- Team collaborative development\n- Code review process', 'Elementary', 'Professional Skills', '/image/course/git.jpg', 'Prof. Wu', 'Prof. Wu is a version control technology expert with 10 years of development experience. Proficient in Git, SVN and other version control tools, and has led the version management of multiple large projects. Teaching style is clear, focusing on practice, and has helped numerous learners master Git skills.', 99.00, 'Professional Skills,Hands-on Practice,Social Learning,Independent Learning,Career Advancement', '[{"title":"Chapter 1: Git Basics","lessons":[{"title":"Git Introduction and Installation","duration":"30 min"},{"title":"Repository Initialization","duration":"40 min"},{"title":"Basic Commands","duration":"60 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 2: Version Management","lessons":[{"title":"Commit History Viewing","duration":"50 min"},{"title":"Version Rollback","duration":"60 min"},{"title":"Working Directory and Staging Area","duration":"70 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 3: Branch Management","lessons":[{"title":"Branch Creation and Switching","duration":"70 min"},{"title":"Branch Merging","duration":"80 min"},{"title":"Branching Strategies","duration":"70 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 4: Remote Collaboration","lessons":[{"title":"Remote Repository Operations","duration":"70 min"},{"title":"Conflict Resolution","duration":"90 min"},{"title":"Pull Request Workflow","duration":"80 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 5: Project Practice","lessons":[{"title":"Personal Project Management","duration":"120 min"},{"title":"Team Collaborative Development","duration":"150 min"}]}]', '["/image/course/git-1.jpg"]', '20 hours', 680, 4.5),
('Algorithms and Data Structures', 'In-depth learning of common algorithms and data structures', 'This course systematically explains the principles and implementation of common algorithms and data structures. From basic data structures, sorting algorithms to graph algorithms, dynamic programming, it comprehensively covers algorithm design skills. Through extensive programming exercises, it helps learners improve their algorithmic thinking and programming abilities.\n\nCourse Content:\n1. Basic data structures (arrays, linked lists, stacks, queues)\n2. Tree and graph structures\n3. Sorting and searching algorithms\n4. Dynamic programming and greedy algorithms\n5. Algorithm complexity analysis\n\nPractice Exercises:\n- LeetCode algorithm problem solutions\n- Algorithm competition training\n- Real project applications', 'Intermediate', 'Programming Development', '/image/course/algorithm.jpg', 'Prof. Zheng', 'Prof. Zheng is an algorithm expert with a doctoral degree and 12 years of algorithm research experience. Has served as an algorithm engineer at several well-known internet companies, proficient in various algorithms and data structures. Teaching style is rigorous, focusing on thinking training, and has helped numerous learners improve their algorithm skills.', 399.00, 'Programming Development,Reading & Writing,Independent Learning,Visual Learning,Academic Advancement', '[{"title":"Chapter 1: Basic Data Structures","lessons":[{"title":"Arrays and Linked Lists","duration":"80 min"},{"title":"Stacks and Queues","duration":"70 min"},{"title":"Hash Tables","duration":"90 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 2: Tree Structures","lessons":[{"title":"Binary Trees","duration":"100 min"},{"title":"Balanced Trees","duration":"90 min"},{"title":"Heap Structures","duration":"80 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 3: Graph Algorithms","lessons":[{"title":"Graph Representation","duration":"80 min"},{"title":"Depth-First Search","duration":"90 min"},{"title":"Shortest Path Algorithms","duration":"100 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 4: Advanced Algorithms","lessons":[{"title":"Dynamic Programming","duration":"120 min"},{"title":"Greedy Algorithms","duration":"100 min"},{"title":"Backtracking Algorithms","duration":"110 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 5: Practice Exercises","lessons":[{"title":"LeetCode Problem Solutions","duration":"200 min"},{"title":"Algorithm Competition Training","duration":"240 min"}]}]', '["/image/course/algorithm-1.jpg","/image/course/algorithm-2.jpg"]', '55 hours', 1400, 4.8),
('Natural Language Processing', 'Learn NLP technology and text analysis', 'This course thoroughly explains natural language processing technology and text analysis methods. From text preprocessing, word vectors to BERT, GPT and other pre-trained models, it comprehensively covers NLP technology. Through multiple practice projects, it helps learners acquire the ability to independently develop NLP applications.\n\nCourse Content:\n1. Text preprocessing techniques\n2. Word vectors and word embeddings\n3. Text classification and sentiment analysis\n4. Sequence labeling and named entity recognition\n5. Pre-trained model applications\n\nProject Practice:\n- Text sentiment analysis system\n- Intelligent question answering system\n- Text generation application', 'Advanced', 'Artificial Intelligence', '/image/course/nlp.jpg', 'Prof. Qian', 'Prof. Qian is an NLP expert with a doctoral degree and 13 years of NLP research experience. Has served as an NLP algorithm expert at several AI companies, proficient in various NLP technologies and pre-trained models. Teaching style is clear and practical, focusing on hands-on experience, and has trained numerous NLP engineers.', 599.00, 'Artificial Intelligence,Reading & Writing,Independent Learning,Visual Learning,Academic Advancement', '[{"title":"Chapter 1: NLP Basics","lessons":[{"title":"Text Preprocessing","duration":"80 min"},{"title":"Tokenization Techniques","duration":"70 min"},{"title":"Part-of-Speech Tagging","duration":"80 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 2: Word Vectors","lessons":[{"title":"Word2Vec","duration":"100 min"},{"title":"GloVe","duration":"90 min"},{"title":"FastText","duration":"80 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 3: Text Classification","lessons":[{"title":"Traditional Machine Learning Methods","duration":"90 min"},{"title":"Deep Learning Models","duration":"110 min"},{"title":"Sentiment Analysis Practice","duration":"100 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 4: Sequence Models","lessons":[{"title":"RNN and LSTM","duration":"110 min"},{"title":"Attention Mechanism","duration":"100 min"},{"title":"Transformer Architecture","duration":"120 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 5: Pre-trained Models","lessons":[{"title":"BERT Model","duration":"130 min"},{"title":"GPT Model","duration":"120 min"},{"title":"Model Fine-tuning","duration":"110 min"}]}]', '["/image/course/nlp-1.jpg","/image/course/nlp-2.jpg","/image/course/nlp-3.jpg"]', '65 hours', 1600, 4.9),
('Web Security Defense', 'Learn web application security defense and vulnerability fixes', 'This course systematically explains web application security defense and vulnerability fix techniques. From common attack methods, security vulnerabilities to defense measures, security testing, it comprehensively covers web security skills. Through multiple practice cases, it helps learners improve web application security.\n\nCourse Content:\n1. Web security fundamentals\n2. Common attack methods (SQL injection, XSS, CSRF, etc.)\n3. Security vulnerability detection\n4. Defense measure implementation\n5. Security testing methods\n\nPractice Cases:\n- Vulnerability scanning and fixes\n- Security hardening practice\n- Penetration testing exercises', 'Intermediate', 'Professional Skills', '/image/course/web-security.jpg', 'Prof. Zhou', 'Prof. Zhou is a web security expert with 14 years of security research experience. Has served as a security engineer at several security companies, proficient in various web security technologies and vulnerability fixes. Teaching style is pragmatic, focusing on hands-on practice, and has helped numerous learners improve their security defense capabilities.', 299.00, 'Professional Skills,Reading & Writing,Independent Learning,Hands-on Practice,Career Advancement', '[{"title":"Chapter 1: Web Security Basics","lessons":[{"title":"Web Security Overview","duration":"50 min"},{"title":"HTTP Protocol Security","duration":"70 min"},{"title":"Authentication and Authorization","duration":"80 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 2: Common Attacks","lessons":[{"title":"SQL Injection Attacks","duration":"90 min"},{"title":"XSS Cross-Site Scripting","duration":"100 min"},{"title":"CSRF Attacks","duration":"80 min"},{"title":"File Upload Vulnerabilities","duration":"90 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 3: Security Defense","lessons":[{"title":"Input Validation","duration":"80 min"},{"title":"Output Encoding","duration":"70 min"},{"title":"Security Configuration","duration":"80 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 4: Security Testing","lessons":[{"title":"Vulnerability Scanning","duration":"90 min"},{"title":"Penetration Testing","duration":"100 min"},{"title":"Security Audit","duration":"80 min"}]},{"title":"Chapter 5: Practice Cases","lessons":[{"title":"Vulnerability Fix Practice","duration":"200 min"},{"title":"Security Hardening Project","duration":"180 min"}]}]', '["/image/course/web-security-1.jpg","/image/course/web-security-2.jpg"]', '40 hours', 1050, 4.7),
